{
  "name": "Weekly manual compact of WeaponX databases",
  "today": "WeaponX is an Access database that the risk book admins use every day. It imports and deletes a lot of data daily, and Access does not free the space, so the file grows to hundreds of MB. In October 2000 Greg Couch asked the six desk heads to have every book admin compact it by hand at least once a week: open the file holding Shift so the main form does not start, run Tools/Database Utilities/Compact Database, wait for it to finish, then use the tool as normal.",
  "change": "Compact each desk's WeaponX file automatically every night instead of having each book admin do it by hand every week.",
  "explanation": "IT sets up a scheduled job (Windows Task Scheduler running Access with the /compact switch, or Microsoft's JetComp utility) that compacts each desk's WeaponX file overnight after the daily run, keeping one backup copy. A simpler alternative is to turn on Access's 'Compact on Close' option in the file. Book admins stop doing the Shift-open and compact routine and stop waiting for it to finish. The files also stay small every day, not just once a week.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "I would like each of your book admins using WeaponX to begin using the \nfollowing procedures at least once/week (if they aren't already)."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "Open the database while holding down on the shift key.  This will open the \ndatabase, but prevent the main form from opening automatically.  Next, the \nadmin should go to Access menu selections and choose Tools/Database \nUtilities/Compact Database.  After the database has completed compacting, you \ncan use the database as normal.",
      "note": "The manual steps each admin repeats: reopen the file in a special way, run the compact, wait for it, then go back to work. A scheduled job does all of this with no one present."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "WeaponX imports and deletes \na lot of data on a daily basis.",
      "note": "The file grows every day, so the compact has to keep being done for as long as the tool is used."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "The Texas WeaponX file that I compacted reduced from 520 MB to 30 MB and one \nfor the west went from 400 MB to 12 MB.",
      "note": "The files are large enough that compacting them takes noticeable time on the PCs of the period."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "Crystal (East desk I believe) already compacts the database on a daily \nbasis.",
      "note": "Some admins already do it every day, so the actual effort is higher than the weekly minimum counted here."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/585.eml",
      "quote": "Try this and see if it does any good.",
      "note": "Giron passed the instructions on to his book admin, Anne Bike, so the procedure reached the admins who do the work."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
    "quote": "at least once/week"
  },
  "minutes": 24
}

