{
  "name": "Searching Houston books for ECC deals to flip to FT-US/CAND-ERMS",
  "today": "Deals with Canadian counterparties that have a master agreement with Enron Canada (ECC) keep landing in Houston TAGG books as ENA deals, including EnronOnline deals placed there automatically. Before invoicing and liquidations, Stacey Vallejo (Calgary) searches the books herself and emails 5 to 7 Houston desk leads asking them to search all their books and flip any such deals to FT-US/CAND-ERMS. Darron Giron forwards each request to between 1 and 7 of his book admins, who each search their books. There is no shared query; people copy each other's ad hoc searches. Deals that are missed hold up invoicing and force liquidations to be re-run. On top of these broad searches, Stacey also sends one-off requests to flip single deals she finds.",
